[0.0, "o", "CONFIGURATION-ONLY DEMO — synthetic credentials; Docker discovery/port checks simulated.\r\n$ ./setup.sh --configure-only\r\n"]
[0.246, "o", "Private Browser setup — Proton VPN on Linux x86-64.\r\nYour VPN credentials stay on this machine. Stopping erases the browser session.\r\nExisting files will be preserved. No host settings will be changed.\r\nUse a Proton WireGuard config downloaded from your own account.\r\nOnly its private key and IPv4 address are imported; DNS, peers and hooks are not applied.\r\nThe VPN server is selected by country using Gluetun’s Proton integration.\r\nIs this a Proton VPN configuration? [y/N] "]
[0.846, "o", "y\r\n"]
